<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30604" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nĕbŭlōsus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		nebula, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of mist</i> or <i>vapor, misty,
				foggy, cloudy, dark</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager si nebulosus est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nebulosum et caliginosum caelum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 1, 25, 60</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nebulosus et roscidus aër,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 7, 18, § 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exhalatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					31, 3, 27, § 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dies nebulosi nubilive,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 2,
					1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Esp.
			of a fine texture, <i>cloud-like</i>, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεφέλαι</span>, nebulosa retia,
					<i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 3,
			5</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>dark, difficult to
				understand</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					20, 3, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
